<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <ScenTitle>Sandbox Scenario #2: East Med A2/AD</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;B style="mso-bidi-font-weight: normal"&gt;&lt;U&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt"&gt;Sides&lt;?xml:namespace prefix = "o" ns = "urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office" /&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/U&gt;&lt;/B&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt"&gt;Blue (NATO) Red (Russia/Syria) and Green (Syrian Rebels)&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt"&gt;This scenario can only be played as &lt;STRONG&gt;Blue. &lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;U&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt"&gt;General Situation&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/U&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt"&gt;On&amp;nbsp;13 January,&amp;nbsp;2016, a Turkish F-16&amp;nbsp;is shot down by Russian fighters after it crossed into Syrian airspace northwest of Idlib. Russia offers no apology and warns Turkey not to allow its fighters to stray into airspace where Russian military forces are conducting operations. In response, the Turks denounce the Russian action and warn against further Russian aggression. Heeding the advice of NATO military commanders, however, Turkey has been allowing Russian aircraft operating against rebel positions&amp;nbsp;in close proximity to the border some wiggle room. Despite the hostile ‘attack’ against its F-16, Turkey&amp;nbsp;allows the small buffer zone to remain in place. However, Adana has announced that it will regard any aircraft that menaces its airspace as hostile and they&amp;nbsp;will be fired upon and brought down. &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt"&gt;For one week afterward, tensions have simmered, but Russian air activity over Syria has been nonexistent. Then on&amp;nbsp;19 January,&amp;nbsp;2016 Russia announces that airstrikes against rebel&amp;nbsp;positions near the Turkish border will resume within 24 hours.&amp;nbsp; The announcement increases the level of tension in the region as the possibility of a confrontation with Turkey increases. NATO has released a statement warning if Russia disregards the sovereignty of Turkish airspace and/or launches an attack on&amp;nbsp;Turkish forces, Article 5 will be invoked immediately. &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt"&gt;NATO will stand beside its Turkish ally. &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;B style="mso-bidi-font-weight: normal"&gt;&lt;U&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt"&gt;Conflict Situation&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/U&gt;&lt;/B&gt;&lt;U&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt"&gt; &lt;SPAN style="mso-spacerun: yes"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/U&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt"&gt;Location: Eastern Mediterranean&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt"&gt;&lt;IMG alt=https://pbs.twimg.com/media/CVuRCOlVAAAyNMb.png src="https://pbs.twimg.com/media/CVuRCOlVAAAyNMb.png"&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt"&gt;The purpose of this scenario will be to examine an air/sea clash between Blue and Red,&amp;nbsp; focusing&amp;nbsp;on&amp;nbsp;Red’s Anti-access/Area Deniability&amp;nbsp;(A2/AD)&amp;nbsp;assets. The scenario will give the player a good idea of Red’s A2/AD&amp;nbsp;advantages and limitations in a near future conflict in the Eastern Med. It also&amp;nbsp;provides the player&amp;nbsp;with the ability to explore Blue’s own capabilities&amp;nbsp; and&amp;nbsp;tactics with regards to neutralizing the A2/AD threat to the airbases and assets in the region such as&amp;nbsp;Incirlik. Last but not least, this scenario&amp;nbsp;will&amp;nbsp;give&amp;nbsp;the player a feel for what operations in the Eastern Med might look like in the early hours of a near-future&amp;nbsp;conflict. &lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt"&gt;For this scenario you are the Blue (NATO) commander. Should hostilities commence because of a Red (Russian) air violation, you will be responsible for retaliation measures and ensuring that Blue air forces maintain air superiority over Turkish airspace. The scope of your response will determine the level of victory or defeat in the scenario. The&amp;nbsp;Commander's Brief will include all of the necessary information and intelligence data you &amp;nbsp;need to put together an effective plan.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt"&gt;This scenario is only 6 hours in duration so time is of the essence. &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt"&gt;Have fun and enjoy! &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt"&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;</ScenDescription>
